      "writtenOn": "2026-03-18T20:07:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m confident there\u0027s no risk of overflow.\n\nLogging rdcosts for the worst case scenario (depth 12, high QP), the highest I\u0027ve seen it go (after applying the bias) is `6,762,139,195`, multiple orders of magnitude below `INT64_MAX` (`9,223,372,036,854,775,807`).\n\nUnless we\u0027re not multiplying rdcosts by like a 1000 or more, and we\u0027re checking for the special \"invalid\" (`INT64_MAX`) rdcost, we should be fine.",
      "parentUuid": "fc208f70_7d12b291",
      "revId": "34eb963ec694e46d9122e2938791be3a4afe302a",
